  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">BRA/25/032 - Forest Finance Leveraged for High Integrity in the Amazon - FOLHA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">Brazil has advanced its climate and forest agenda, but subnational jurisdictions still face institutional, technical, and regulatory barriers to implementing high-integrity jurisdictional REDD+ programs at scale. These gaps limit access to sustainable, results-based forest finance and weaken safeguards, governance, and credibility. Between 2026 and 2029, UNDP, with support from NICFI, will provide targeted technical assistance to strengthen state-level readiness for J-REDD+ implementation aligne</narrative>
  </description>
